{"agent":"bg58","data":{"auto":false,"dedupe":{"answer":"extends","candidates":[{"id":"B-chunk-rerun-drops-peer-findings","score":0.660906684},{"id":"fix-B-chunk-rerun-drops-peer-findings","score":0.610872366}],"score":0.660906684,"target":"B-chunk-rerun-drops-peer-findings"},"relation":"extends","score":0.660906684,"text":"Does merge_rerun drop a reviewer's finding that a DIFFERENT reviewer raised in a re-run chunk?\nmerge_rerun rebuilds prior findings as Finding objects that drop the reviewer, and filters prior chunk_findings with no reviewer check, so a --chunk re-run of reviewer b drops a HIGH raised by reviewer a in that chunk.\nrunner.merge_rerun keeps a prior finding only when its chunk is not re-run or not in this cut; the Finding dataclass carried no reviewer, so a finding did not say whose it was.","who":"bg58"},"id":"e8bde421a5df2867d1314a1fe","kind":"record.extended","lamport":152204,"schema":1,"subject":"B-chunk-rerun-drops-peer-findings","ts":"2026-11-08T03:23:52.283367Z"}
